rt with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"SketchUp"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Illustrator/InDesign"},{"text":"Basic GIS awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a small:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neighborhood park"},{"text":"Courtyard"},{"text":"Campus landscape"},{"text":"Residential garden"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Landscape & Environmental Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"The focus should shift toward understanding how land, vegetation, water and built form interact."},{"type":"h","text":"Landscape Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Landscape composition"},{"text":"Planting design"},{"text":"Hardscape"},{"text":"Softscape"},{"text":"Site planning"},{"text":"Landscape materials"},{"text":"Garden design"},{"text":"Outdoor circulation"},{"text":"Public-space principles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ecology"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Native vegetation"},{"text":"Biodiversity"},{"text":"Urban ecosystems"},{"text":"Soil health"},{"text":"Habitat"},{"text":"Microclimate"},{"text":"Ecological corridors"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Site Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn fundamentals of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Grading"},{"text":"Drainage"},{"text":"Stormwater"},{"text":"Retaining walls"},{"text":"Paving"},{"text":"Steps and ramps"},{"text":"Site utilities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Landscape Architecture Specialization"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student should start thinking at urban scale."},{"type":"h","text":"Urban Landscape Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Urban parks"},{"text":"Plazas"},{"text":"Streetscapes"},{"text":"Pedestrian corridors"},{"text":"Greenways"},{"text":"Urban forests"},{"text":"Waterfronts"},{"text":"Transit-oriented public spaces"},{"text":"Institutional campuses"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Public Realm"},{"type":"p","text":"Under